      },
      "displayName": "Chris Wilper",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3Ae25d94d0-bd50-4c2c-906c-14cdf85801fb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "[Followup from Sourceforge Tracker]",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Followup Submitter: sjw46",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Logged In: YES ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "user_id=1709161",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Originator: YES",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Background:",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "To protect against repeatedly attempting to ingest the same object when",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "iterating the lowlevel objects directory, the rebuilder keeps track of all PIDs",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "it has ingested so far.  If it encounters one it has already seen, it skips it",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "and prints a warning.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Problem:",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "For large repositories, it's impractical to store all \"seen\" PIDs in memory. ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Therefore, a memory-efficient int-based set is used in conjunction with",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "String.hashCode().",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "A hash collision arises when String.hashCode() returns the same value for two",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "different PIDs.  This causes the second one to be skipped by the rebuilder.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
