      },
      "displayName": "Chris Wilper",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3Ae25d94d0-bd50-4c2c-906c-14cdf85801fb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p><span class=\"error\">&#91;Followup from Sourceforge Tracker&#93;</span><br/>\nFollowup Submitter: sjw46<br/>\nLogged In: YES <br/>\nuser_id=1709161<br/>\nOriginator: YES</p>\n\n<p>Background:</p>\n\n<p>To protect against repeatedly attempting to ingest the same object when<br/>\niterating the lowlevel objects directory, the rebuilder keeps track of all PIDs<br/>\nit has ingested so far.  If it encounters one it has already seen, it skips it<br/>\nand prints a warning.</p>\n\n<p>Problem:</p>\n\n<p>For large repositories, it's impractical to store all \"seen\" PIDs in memory. <br/>\nTherefore, a memory-efficient int-based set is used in conjunction with<br/>\nString.hashCode().</p>\n\n<p>A hash collision arises when String.hashCode() returns the same value for two<br/>\ndifferent PIDs.  This causes the second one to be skipped by the rebuilder.</p>",
     "created": "12/Mar/07 5:32 PM",
